# Sidecars are built (`tendril`) or downloaded (`opencode`) into this directory, never committed.
#
# Tauri bundles whatever it finds here, and it resolves a sidecar by target triple
# (`binary-name-<triple>{.exe}`). Committed placeholders for the triples a given runner is not
# building therefore ship *inside the installer* for every other platform — which is how four
# 163-byte "stub running" shell scripts came to be part of the release. Keep the directory, keep
# nothing in it.
#
# `scripts/fetch-opencode-sidecar.sh` populates `opencode-*`; the release workflow's
# "Build companion CLI binary" step populates `tendril-*`.
*
!.gitignore
